ich ${x}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are vertical). So, to find it, we set the first equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n-2x+4y=0\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}x\n$$\n\n- The $y$-nullcline is a line for which ${y}^{′}=0$ (i.e., the tangents to trajectories are horizontal). So, to find it, we set the second equation of the system equal to $0:$\n\n$$\nx-y=0\\,⇒\\,y=x\n$$\n\nPlotting these in the phase space, we obtain the following:\n\n![](images/19/19c33a634af36765142e2f4b85df1b9209d3f1abf105a131b629b3249bd91c2c.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306098 #edb/ref 1080 "images/7d/7d6d07e888cd0dd55fd37a8a620c8be054eee0e6abc170133a4188667dcc65b4.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306098 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306098 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "61df7f22-6ffa-57a8-9916-b16cd0e6d7a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306363 #edb/ref 1080 "images/6e/6e2e7d099ed478a259b241320481c4beacda56cea59adc2c7314636f42e79f3e.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306363 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306363 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7e88af57-d11c-5f11-ae26-c363739c22eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306572 #edb/ref 1080 "images/0e/0eff17334f3ca56152140bfefaf10a3169ad34a8b6e1e3322bd7fb03963c2338.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306572 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306572 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9713628a-50bc-55aa-9c55-eaff442a58c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306926 #edb/ref 1080 "images/f1/f128b9d7ed44f4b0e7c40177e7198c0593f6ff9b262fae153ffbfad963d00873.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306926 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306926 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "be682b22-dd95-5509-aae0-426f78a07495" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186307022 #edb/ref 1080 "images/f9/f906ea39089da431a1b86d3e7b8ab68ff7a287f8c4af4c3a5b9c1117eff2b57b.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186307022 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186307022 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c90626e8-1636-5700-ba43-5e845dd15842" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186306098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186306363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186306572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186306926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308106 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186307022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308106 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308106 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308106 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186306572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308106 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b8399834-d23a-59a9-8ff6-060b534eecb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308342 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308342 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332932" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308342 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308342 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/83/83147b64f8f34d43b9503186f3d2df5926ce119953c80d10f4cd8b8ef94bfcfc.png)\n\nA sketch of the phase space with nullclines and the corresponding direction field of tangents to the solutions of a system of differential equations is shown above (the tangents are not drawn to scale). Which of the following could represent the trajectory starting at the point marked on the graph?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308342 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2dfbad27-2f3a-51d2-ab57-9054aa8268d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308342 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's sketch the trajectory.\n\n- We start at the given point, going along with the flow (upward and slightly to the right) until the trajectory intersects the $x$-nullcline, where the tangents are vertical.\n\n![](images/6d/6d897c2e9249447cc2d0c902a592d04442b0928c315163b6ab80cff288c84657.png)\n\n- Next, the flow continues going upward but then starts turning  to the left.\n\n![](images/be/bed6896ecc0edcdb157b648108d403e1b8e29463d9f61aa0e0c26e8f5e2dd8c6.png)\n\n- After that, the trajectory continues upward and slightly to the left, suggesting that it may converge to the origin\n\n![](images/cc/cc53577a278595e5f0155119aa5eb1a7b27ec01847a6daa1ba6ade6792c5f5e9.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390992 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186390993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390992 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332619" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390992 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390992 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x(t)={e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem and its solution given above. What is the tangent vector to the solution curve at the point corresponding to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390992 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "be9877ee-3abb-5c56-bc3e-693bac7c1ef7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390992 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the $xy$-coordinate plane is called the *phase plane* of the system. A particular solution of an initial value problem is called a *trajectory* (or *orbit*).\n\nFirst, we compute the point that corresponds to $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ on the given trajectory:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & ={e}^{-2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation of our system, we obtain the tangent vector to the trajectory.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2(\\frac{1}{3})+0(6) \\\\ 0(\\frac{1}{3})+1(6)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390993 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390993 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390993 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390993 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390993 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390993 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390993 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390993 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186390995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390993 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "491749e3-5dfc-5a6a-8c20-a36eb891b6a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390994 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390994 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390994 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9c1207d6-660a-5878-9696-b2a6f678e57f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390995 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390995 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390995 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c326cefc-3d33-51f6-b6f0-7a69d00ee5f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390996 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390996 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390996 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bb18a87c-c989-5a99-a62f-c5acf7e387f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390997 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}\